                    "demo": "https://demo.getgrav.org/helios/",
                    "keywords": "grav, theme, documentation, tailwind, docs, api, premium",
                    "bugs": "https://github.com/getgrav/grav-premium-issues/labels/helios",
                    "license": "https://getgrav.org/premium/license",
                    "tag_name": "2.1.16",
                    "date": "2026-08-11T19:22:27Z",
                    "release_type": "stable",
                    "zipball_url": "https://getgrav.org/download/themes/helios/2.1.16",
                    "repository": "https://github.com/trilbymedia/grav-theme-helios",
                    "premium": {
                        "permalink": "grav-premium-helios",
                        "checkout_url": "https://licensing.getgrav.org/buy/grav-premium-helios",
                        "button": "Buy Now",
                        "filename": "grav-theme-helios"
                    },
                    "slug": "helios",
                    "install_path": "user/themes/helios",
                    "content_sha256": "1865278379ae5e995e290fc6834a1f23b15205c7f96638bf39b14ae6731c65c6",
                    "screenshot": "themes-helios.jpg",
                    "changelog": {
                        "2.1.16": {
                            "date": "08/11/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#bugfix)\n    * The file tree shortcode keeps its line breaks and indentation when you switch to Editor Pro and back, instead of being flattened onto one line ([getgrav/grav-premium-issues#614](https://github.com/getgrav/grav-premium-issues/issues/614)).\n"
                        },
                        "2.1.15": {
                            "date": "07/17/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed the PHP debug bar not rendering (and its \"PhpDebugBar is not defined\" console error) by outputting the default `head` JS asset group, which core and plugins use and the theme was previously dropping\n"
                        },
                        "2.1.14": {
                            "date": "07/13/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#bugfix)\n    * The login, registration, and profile pages now render inside the theme layout instead of showing just a heading with no form\n"
                        },
                        "2.1.13": {
                            "date": "07/08/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#new)\n    * Added a `tailwind4:` contract to the theme config, so the [Tailwind4 plugin](https://github.com/getgrav/grav-plugin-tailwind4) can compile the theme's CSS from PHP with no Node/npm toolchain. The npm build scripts still work; both produce the same output\n"
                        },
                        "2.1.12": {
                            "date": "07/06/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed the documentation version (sidebar navigation and version badge) being misdetected on any page that is the configured `system.home.alias`. Grav collapses such a page's `route()` to `/`, which hid the version prefix and forced a fall-through to `default_version` \u2014 so with a non-default `default_version`, pages under another version rendered the default version's navigation and badge. Version detection now reads `rawRoute()`, which always carries the real `/<version>/...` path\n"
                        },
                        "2.1.11": {
                            "date": "07/05/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed wide tables no longer scrolling horizontally on narrow screens/mobile. Content tables are now their own horizontal scroll container (`display:block` with `overflow-x:auto`), so oversized tables scroll instead of squishing while narrow tables still fill the full content width [#599](https://github.com/getgrav/grav-premium-issues/issues/599)\n"
                        },
                        "2.1.10": {
                            "date": "07/01/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed the `[doc-image]` lightbox opening the raw image file instead of the zoom overlay. The 2.1.9 fix for #598 added a capture-phase click guard that stopped propagation on any link to a media file, which fired before the lightbox link's own bubble-phase handler could `preventDefault()`. The guard now leaves `hx-boost=\"false\"` links (including the lightbox link) alone, since HTMX never boosts them anyway [#598](https://github.com/getgrav/grav-premium-issues/issues/598)\n"
                        },
                        "2.1.9": {
                            "date": "06/30/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed HTMX navigation hijacking links to media files, so clicking a local PDF or other attachment now opens it in the browser instead of dumping its contents into the page [#598](https://github.com/getgrav/grav-premium-issues/issues/598)\n"
                        },
                        "2.1.8": {
                            "date": "06/18/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Hardened HTMX back/forward navigation against browser-specific history failures (notably Brave, where Shields can partition or clear `localStorage` and leave htmx's history snapshot cache empty). Set `htmx-config` `refreshOnHistoryMiss: true` so a history cache miss falls back to a full page reload instead of a silent AJAX swap that could update the URL without updating the content [#594](https://github.com/getgrav/grav-premium-issues/issues/594)\n"
                        },
                        "2.1.7": {
                            "date": "06/16/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed the back/forward button losing the page chrome (sidebar, header, TOC) during HTMX-boosted navigation. On a history cache miss htmx re-fetches the URL and replaces the whole `<body>`, but the theme only checked for the `HX-Request` header and returned the chrome-less content partial. It now excludes history-restore requests (`HX-History-Restore-Request`) so the back button receives the full page. Also added `Vary: HX-Request, HX-History-Restore-Request` so Grav's long `Cache-Control` can't let a cached partial poison a later full navigation\n"
                        },
                        "2.1.6": {
                            "date": "06/14/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed the left navigation menu and version switcher not showing when Helios was used as a custom copy or inherited child theme [#592](https://github.com/getgrav/grav-premium-issues/issues/592)\n"
                        },
                        "2.1.5": {
                            "date": "06/04/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed a fatal `Unknown \"native_name\" function` Twig error that took down the whole site when Helios was used without the Langswitcher plugin installed. The header partials included `partials/langswitcher.html.twig` unconditionally, and although the partial guards its body with `{% if langswitcher is defined %}`, Twig still parses the `native_name()` call at compile time and throws because the function is only registered by the Langswitcher plugin. Wrapped the `{% include %}` in `header.html.twig` and `header-simple.html.twig` with `{% if langswitcher is defined %}` so the partial is never compiled when the plugin is absent\n"
                        },
                        "2.1.4": {
                            "date": "05/26/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed `[doc-steps]` rendering the native `<ol>` decimal marker alongside the custom step-number badge. The `.prose ol` rule was overriding `.doc-steps`'s `list-none` due to higher selector specificity; qualified the selector as `ol.doc-steps` so the list marker stays suppressed inside prose content [#584](https://github.com/getgrav/grav-premium-issues/issues/584)\n"
                        },
                        "2.1.3": {
                            "date": "05/20/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed `[doc-image]` rendering as a broken image when `src` referenced a page-local file (e.g. `feathers-mcgraw.webp`), a `../`-relative path, or a Grav stream (`theme://`, `user://`, `image://`). The shortcode now resolves `src` through Grav's standard path resolution (`Excerpts::processLinkHtml`), matching how markdown image paths are handled, while deliberately bypassing the Medium image pipeline so animated GIFs and animated WebPs stay animated [#581](https://github.com/getgrav/grav-premium-issues/issues/581)\n    * Fixed `[doc-image]` lightbox issues with animated GIFs (and other images): clicking a lightbox image inside the HTMX-boosted main region was being intercepted by `hx-boost`, causing the page to AJAX-navigate to the raw image URL. The lightbox link now opts out of boost. Also fixed the close button being un-clickable when the click landed on the inner SVG strokes [#581](https://github.com/getgrav/grav-premium-issues/issues/581)\n    "
                        },
                        "2.1.2": {
                            "date": "05/19/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#improved)\n    * Reworked content-width model so `navigation.content_width` now represents the total content area (article plus the TOC slot). The article automatically fills the freed-up space when the TOC is hidden, instead of leaving a fixed gap. Default bumped from `768` to `1040` so existing reading widths stay the same when the TOC is visible; allowed range widened to `800`\u2013`1600`.\n    * Existing configs with a saved `content_width` below `900` are auto-promoted to the new total-width interpretation, so older sites keep rendering at the same article width without manual changes.\n    * Unified the regular Twig and HTMX render paths into a single `partials/swap-body.html.twig` partial \u2014 both full page loads and HTMX swaps now produce identical inner HTML by construction, preventing future drift between the two. Per-template files (`doc`, `chapter`, `api-endpoint`, `api-collection`, `error`) collapsed to extends-only since the shared partial handles template dispatch.\n1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed HTMX navigation rendering the article at the wrong width after the content-width rework. The width rule now lives in Twig and is shipped to the client via `htmx-nav-state`, so the JS no longer re-derives it.\n    * Fixed `navigation.content_when_toc_hidden: contained` being ignored on HTMX-navigated pages (the JS was always treating TOC-hidden as expand-content).\n    * Fixed pages without any qualifying TOC headings (e.g. pages with just an H1) rendering the article at the narrower with-TOC width on full page loads, while HTMX swaps to the same page rendered correctly at the expanded width. `base.html.twig` now pre-renders the TOC partial and checks whether it produced any content, applying the same expand-when-empty rule the HTMX JS already used.\n    * Fixed `[doc-image]` lightbox issues with animated GIFs (and other images): clicking a lightbox image inside the HTMX-boosted main region was being intercepted by `hx-boost`, causing the page to AJAX-navigate to the raw image URL. The lightbox link now opts out of boost. Also fixed the close button being un-clickable when the click landed on the inner SVG strokes [#581](https://github.com/getgrav/grav-premium-issues/issues/581)\n"
                        },
                        "2.1.1": {
                            "date": "04/24/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#new)\n    * Added `navigation.content_when_toc_hidden` theme option (`full` | `contained`) controlling how content is laid out when the on-page TOC is hidden. Default `full` expands content into the reserved TOC space so the content's horizontal position stays the same as pages that have a TOC (no layout jump). `contained` keeps the content at its configured width, leaving a blank gutter where the TOC would be. Overridable per page via `navigation.content_when_toc_hidden` in page frontmatter.\n1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed `#toc-layout` collapsing to `max-content` on short pages, causing the content to appear as a narrow centered column instead of filling the configured content width [#566](https://github.com/getgrav/grav-premium-issues/issues/566)\n    * Fixed breadcrumb walker pushing Grav's internal pages root node, producing a stray \"Pages\" crumb between the home icon and the current page title on any top-level non-home page [#567](https://github.com/getgrav/grav-premium-issues/issues/567)\n    * Fixed breadcrumb \"home\" link and version-switcher fallback URL dropping the multisite environment prefix on subfolder installs that use Grav's `setup.php` multi-site pattern [#565](https://github.com/getgrav/grav-premium-issues/issues/565)\n"
                        },
                        "2.1.0": {
                            "date": "04/24/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#new)\n    * Added a new **collection** style API format that works well for large API documentation as it bundles an entire endpoint (POST/PUT/GET/PATCH/DELETE, etc) into a single page.\n"
                        },
                        "2.0.5": {
                            "date": "03/06/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#new)\n    * Added language switcher dropdown in the header when the `langswitcher` plugin is active and multiple languages are configured. Displays languages in their native names with a compact globe-icon trigger.\n"
                        },
                        "2.0.4": {
                            "date": "03/06/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#improved)\n  * Added a simple 'extends' tempalte for `docs.html.twig` to extend the Helios provided `doc.html.twig` template\n1. [](#bugfix)\n   * Added a check for yetisearch-pro's branding toggle in Helios' template override\n"
                        },
                        "2.0.3": {
                            "date": "03/01/2026",
                            "content": "1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed ToC not showing when page relies on theme config instead of explicit frontmatter, caused by `theme_var()` inheriting `toc_position: hidden` from parent pages [#546](https://github.com/getgrav/grav-premium-issues/issues/546)\n    * Fixed HTMX navigation not showing ToC when initial page has ToC hidden (container was never rendered in DOM) [#546](https://github.com/getgrav/grav-premium-issues/issues/546)\n"
                        }
                    },
                    "download": "https://getgrav.org/download/themes/helios/2.1.16"
                },
